Package: HSMap
Type: Package
Title: Maternal Linkage Mapping in Open-Pollinated Diploid Families
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marcelo", "Mollinari", email = "mmollina@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kim", "McKeever", role = "aut"),
    person("Molly", "Irvin", role = "aut"),
    person("Fikret", "Isik", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Builds maternal linkage maps in open-pollinated (unknown-sire) diploid
             half-sib families: one known, genotyped dam, many offspring, and
             unobserved fathers. Chromosome-wide maps are fitted with a source-aware
             hidden Markov model whose state pairs the transmitted maternal homolog
             with a paternal source state, so that persistent paternal
             haplotype-sharing tracts (as arise when some pollen parents are related
             to the dam) are modelled explicitly instead of being absorbed into the
             maternal recombination map. Setting the sharing-entry rate to zero
             recovers the simpler population-mode estimator exactly. The package also
             provides two-point recombination estimation, dam phase assembly, marker
             grouping and ordering, framework-map construction, and per-offspring
             maternal inheritance probabilities; maps are fitted within resolved
             phase blocks, and no-linkage intervals are reported as gaps rather than
             large centimorgan distances. Extensions that pool several dams under one
             shared map (via a joint EM) and that handle known-sire full-sib crosses
             are included and documented as forthcoming.
